{
  "id": "appsdk-collab-control-plane-reset",
  "version": "0.2.1",
  "description": "SESE control-plane reset graph. It captures the routes level, the only level that inventories duplicate pane claimants and has a postcondition to verify. It authorizes one explicit reset level, proves exclusivity, inventories the exact retire set including duplicate pane claimants, retires the selected state transactionally, verifies the postcondition by replaying the daemon's own reader, and emits one audit receipt. The project and host levels share the inventory, archive, retire, and receipt nodes but never call verify_retirement, and the routes level never stages an archive or rebuilds a baseline, so those two nodes are no-ops there; the level selects the inventory and retire set, not the topology. Failure terminals are bound to the node that produces them, because dagpipe requires an audited SESE graph to declare exactly one output arc, so a terminal cannot also be a sink node. authorize_reset produces RESET_LEVEL_REQUIRED, RESET_LEVEL_FLAG_MISMATCH, RESET_AUTHORIZATION_REQUIRED, RESET_STORAGE_ROOT_REQUIRED, and RESET_STORAGE_ROOT_INVALID. prove_exclusivity produces RESET_DAEMON_LIVE. inventory_control_plane produces RESET_KEEP_REQUIRED (carrying the candidate list), RESET_INDEX_ROOT_UNRESOLVED, and RESET_PROJECT_HOLDS_HOST_INDEX. verify_retirement produces RESET_VERIFY_FAILED, after restoring the whole journal file from its pre-image snapshot. Every terminal leaves the source untouched.",
